{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 English tooling differs, but the {\b logical procedure} is what we want to keep parallel.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 3.1 Annotate a slice (A \u8594? B \u8594? C)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab {\b Build inputs} \u8212- KWIC / snippet records with provenance ({\f1 corpus}, {\f1 date}, {\f1 target_word}, {\f1 context_text}, ideally {\f1 text_regime}).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab {\b Run or label Step A} \u8212- food entity? metaphor? early dropout when out of scope.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab {\b Run or label Step B} \u8212- pick one macro-frame + a short lexical trigger ({\f1 lexical_unit}).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab {\b Run or label Step C} \u8212- fill {\b only} the roles for that frame; leave empty when not stated in the snippet.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab {\b Keep provenance} on every row \u8212- era/corpus are fields, not separate pipelines.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Automated Dutch path: {\f1 trifecta-batch} (LLM + structured Pydantic outputs). Hand path: gold CSV / notebook lab.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 3.2 Grow hand gold (quota batches)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Dutch Step 5 runbook ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "GOLD_LABELLING.md#step-5-runbook--cooking_creation-qualia-m10"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
GOLD_LABELLING.md
}}}
):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab {\b Export a bounded batch} \u8212- e.g.\u160?clear-frame miner \u8594? ~30 {\f1 COOKING_CREATION} candidates ({\f1 export_clear_frame_examples.py}).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab {\b Hand-label} in the notebook lab ({\f1 cooking_stepc_gold_lab}) \u8212- snippet-first; Step A/B + COOKING Step C fields; mark {\f1 labelled=true}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab {\b Merge \u8594? import} \u8594? {\f1 gold_labelling_all.csv} \u8594? {\f1 gold.parquet} / {\f1 gold.jsonl}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab {\b Sampling discipline} (policy): cap per lemma; sample by regime \u215? phenomenon; no new core gold with {\f1 UNKNOWN} regime; disagreement CSVs for adjudication only (not auto-relabel).\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs28 3.3 Evaluate and calibrate\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Rebuild gold eval inputs \u8594? {\f1 trifecta-batch} on the gold slice \u8594? {\f1 gold_predictions.jsonl}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab {\f1 trifecta-eval} \u8212- Step A/B (report {\b per} {\f1 text_regime} first) + Step C:\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Exact} normalized string match (strict).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Soft} containment (pred may be longer than gold if one string contains the other).\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab {\b Review} gold vs pred ({\f1 step_c_review} notebook / CSV) \u8594? pick few-shot exemplars \u8594? wire into Step C prompts \u8594? re-batch gold only.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab {\b Analysis export} \u8212- flatten batch JSONL \u8594? parquet ({\f1 trifecta_analysis}) with an explicit {\b uncertainty} note: Step C is an LLM hypothesis unless the row is hand gold.\sa180\par}
